192.168.197.2>ipf

NAME
     ipf - firewall configuration

192.168.197.2>.

SYNOPSIS
     ipf [-6frnmDEF:P:SVZ] [rule or filename]

DESCRIPTION
     ipf configures firewall rules. Default operation is to add
     a rule. Use the -r flag to remove a rule. ipfirewall can also be used
     to display or flush the rule, state or log tables.

     -m           MAC filter rule
     -6           Rule applies to IPv6
     -r           Remove rule
     -f           Get rules from file
     -n           Do not change the rule table, just check rule syntax
     -D           Disable the firewall
     -E           Enable the firewall
     -F [rsluag<id>]   Flush table(s)     r=rules s=state l=log u=user a=all g<id>=rules in specific group
     -P [rsluag<id>]   Display table(s)   r=rules s=state l=log u=user a=all g<id>=rules in specific group
     -S           Display statistics
     -V           Show firewall version
     -Z           Clear statistics

IP FILTER RULE SYNTAX
     [@<index>] <pass/block [return-rst | return-icmp[-as-dest][(val)]> <in/out> [log [first]]
     [limit [!] <val> burst <val>] [quick] [on [!] <interface[+]>] [pktflags <val>[/mask]]
     [tos <val>[/mask]] [ttl <val>] [proto <val>] <address scope> [icmp-type <val>] [flags <val>[/mask]]
     [with [no] <frag|ipopts>] [keep state | keep ifstate [limited] | keep ipsecstate] [head|group <val>]
     [userdef <id> [paramstring]]

IP FILTER ADDRESS SCOPE
     <all | from <[!] any|me|ipaddr[/mask]> [port <op> <val>] to <[!] any|me|ipaddr[/mask]> [port <op> <val>]>>

MAC FILTER RULE SYNTAX
     [@<index>] <pass/block <in/out> [log [first]] [limit [!] <val> burst <val>] [quick] [on [!] <interface[+]>] <address scope> [mac-type <val>] [802_2] [802_2-dsap [!] <val>] [802_2-ssap [!] <val>]
     [802_2-snap-vendor [!] <val>] [802_2-snap-type [!] <val>] [head|group <val>]  [userdef <id> [paramstring]]

MAC FILTER ADDRESS SCOPE
     <all | from <[!] any|me|macaddr[/mask]> to <[!] any|me|ipaddr[/mask]>>

RETURN VALUES
     The ipfirewall command will exit with 0 on success, and non-zero on errors.
